  "answer": "Citation complaints declined significantly from Q1 to Q2. Q1 saw a sharp increase in citation-error tickets [NL-010#NL-010-S05]. Ticket data shows a steady drop from Q1 (January 72, February 79, March 88) to Q2 (April 42, May 31, June 24) [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. The April release—which bound document metadata directly to vector chunks and improved chunking/re-ranking—drove this reduction [NL-011#NL-011-S05], [NL-016#NL-016-S04]. However, remaining tickets in May and June are almost entirely linked to scanned, image-only PDFs, where citation anchors fail or point to the start of the file [NL-011#NL-011-S05], [NL-016#NL-016-S04].\n\nThe planned product work directly addressing the remaining scanned-document problem is the **Advanced OCR Pipeline**. It is targeted to launch a pilot by August 2026 [NL-010#NL-010-S10] and is scheduled for release in August 2026 to automatically extract text and layout structures from scanned files, enabling page-specific citations [NL-024#NL-024-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
